# The Bellic tab for an armed and then a wounded protagonist.
#
# --weapons puts an arming sword in the right hand and a round shield in the left, so the tab
# shows two weapon blocks and the shield's guard reads as defence dice rather than an attack.
# `wound protagonist 5` then lays five wounds from the catalogue — seeded, so the same five every run —
# and the ears' among them costs initiative, which the tab marks ↓ beside the number the fight reads.
# --organs trunk=5 gives the body the hit points to carry five wounds and live.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --weapons --grant-mm brawling:2,swordsmanship:2 --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --period noon --organs trunk=5

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 45

# --- armed ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
manage Bellic
wait 1
expect Arming Sword
expect Round Shield
expect long blade
expect Cover
expect def
expect-not Wounds weigh on this body
dump

manage Bellic Cover
wait 1
expect added to your defence
dump

# --- wounded -------------------------------------------------------------------------
manage
wound protagonist 5
manage Bellic
wait 1
expect Wounds weigh on this body
expect 1d6 + 1 ↓
dump

quit
